<h1>HOPE LABS<br>Web Platform Proposal & Solar Power Calculator Project</h1>

<table class="header-table">
  <tr>
    <td><strong>Prepared By:</strong> Hope Labs</td>
    <td><strong>Client:</strong> Sara Power Solutions</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>Project:</strong> Solar Catalog & Sizing Engine</td>
    <td><strong>Domain:</strong> sarapowersolutions.com</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>Base Investment:</strong> 45,000 ETB</td>
    <td><strong>Payment Terms:</strong> 2-Phase Split (50% / 50%)</td>
  </tr>
</table>

<h2>1. Executive Summary</h2>
<p>Hope Labs is pleased to present this technical proposal for the design, development, and deployment of the Sara Power Solutions web platform. The platform integrates a modern luxury product showcase with an advanced interactive Solar Power Engineering Calculator to deliver a high-converting digital experience for your customers.</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Luxury Kith-Style Showcase:</strong> A mobile-first, edge-to-edge cinematic product catalog featuring a category drill-down system, dark/light mode, and instant WhatsApp/Telegram lead generation.</li>
  <li><strong>FR-2 Solar Sizing Engine:</strong> An interactive dual-mode tool allowing customers to enter their household appliance loads (or direct kW limits) and receive mathematically matched inverter, battery, and panel recommendations. It includes one-click PDF engineering report generation.</li>
  <li><strong>Dynamic Admin Portal:</strong> A highly secure dashboard allowing admins to control the entire platform without a developer. This includes uploading hero carousel banners, managing the product inventory with strict technical attributes, and modifying branding and social media telemetry.</li>
  <li><strong>Cloud Hosting Infrastructure:</strong> Next.js 14 full-stack framework deployed on Vercel's Global Edge Network, backed by a Supabase PostgreSQL cloud database featuring Realtime data synchronization.</li>
</ul>

<h2>2. Household Solar Power Calculator Specification</h2>
<p>The calculator acts as an automated digital engineer, simplifying decision-making for customers seeking solar solutions:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Interactive Data Input:</strong> Customers either select their household appliances and runtimes (Checklist Mode) or input their precise peak kW demand and daily kWh energy requirements (Direct Mode).</li>
  <li><strong>Algorithmic Matching:</strong> The engine calculates systemic efficiency losses and queries the live Supabase inventory to find exact matches for Inverter capacity (kVA), Battery storage (kWh), and Panel wattage (Wp).</li>
  <li><strong>Intelligent Packaging:</strong> It generates 3 distinct tiered packages (Essential Backup, Hybrid Kit, Master Kit) allowing clients to choose their level of investment, and provides a direct 'Send Inquiry' bridge to WhatsApp.</li>
</ul>

<h2>3. Investment & Payment Milestones</h2>
<p>The total base investment for the complete platform is 45,000 ETB, structured in 2 equal milestones:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Phase 1: Kickoff Deposit (50%) - 22,500 ETB</strong><br>Paid prior to development start. Covers database schema, product attribute setup, UI/UX design wireframing, and core catalog engineering.</li>
  <li><strong>Phase 2: Final Go-Live (50%) - 22,500 ETB</strong><br>Paid upon reviewing and approving the live staging demo prior to pointing the primary domain live.</li>
</ul>

<h2>4. Scope Revisions & Additional Features Policy</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Included in Base Price:</strong> Standard review feedback, minor design adjustments, text edits, and layout refinements during the Phase 2 demo.</li>
  <li><strong>Major Scope Additions:</strong> If future feedback introduces completely new modules outside the agreed scope (e.g., payment gateway integration, custom mobile apps, multi-vendor logistics), these will be quoted transparently as add-ons prior to implementation.</li>
</ul>

<h2>5. System Maintenance & Management Options</h2>
<p>Sara Power Solutions can select one of the following two ongoing management models after launch:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Option A: Managed Service & Maintenance (Recommended)</strong><br>Hope Labs retains administrative management on Vercel & Supabase. Hope Labs provides uptime monitoring, database backups, content updates, and technical support under a monthly/quarterly retainer.</li>
  <li><strong>Option B: Client Ownership with Admin Access (Hybrid)</strong><br>Sara Power Solutions registers its own Vercel & Supabase accounts for 100% legal ownership and hosting billing. Hope Labs is invited as an Admin/Developer to perform regular updates and maintenance.</li>
</ul>

